    "result_text": "Done. **BUILD SUCCESS** \u2014 all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe business-day roll for the registration date now skips public holidays in addition to weekends.\n\nI updated `rollToBusinessDay` in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` (the single place that adjusts an owner's `registrationDate` on save):\n\n- Added a `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` constant with the fixed list: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Changed the roll from a single-step weekend switch to a loop that advances one day at a time while the date is a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a listed public holiday \u2014 so an adjusted date landing on a holiday now rolls forward to the next non-holiday business day (correctly chaining, e.g. a holiday falling on a Friday would continue past the weekend).\n\nThis matches the invariant asserted by the acceptance test (`toBusinessDay`/`HOLIDAYS` in `AcceptanceBase`), which the suite confirms green.",
