    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic:\n\n- The `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` constant is a `Set.of(...)` placed right next to the method that uses it, giving O(1) membership checks and a single obvious place to maintain the list.\n- Extracting `isWeekend(...)` cleanly separates the \"is this a weekend\" concern from the roll loop, and the switch fall-through (`SATURDAY`/`SUNDAY` \u2192 `true`) is a natural Java idiom.\n- Replacing the special-cased `plusDays(2)`/`plusDays(1)` arithmetic with a uniform `while (...) date = date.plusDays(1)` loop is the right generalization \u2014 it correctly composes weekend-skipping and holiday-skipping without needing to reason about how many days to jump, and it naturally handles adjacent holidays/weekends.\n- The Javadoc was updated to accurately describe the new behavior.\n\nLogic sits in the right unit (a private helper on the service that already owned `rollToBusinessDay`), nothing is duplicated, and no class or method is becoming a catch-all. A maintainer of this codebase would find it natural.",
